# NLP Text Classification & Model Benchmarking Pipeline

## Project Overview

This project implements an end-to-end Natural Language Processing (NLP) and machine learning pipeline for classifying textual comments, such as user feedback and social media comments, into six categories:

- Positive
- Negative
- Interrogative
- Imperative
- Corrective
- Miscellaneous

The project focuses on text preprocessing, feature engineering, comparative machine learning, hyperparameter optimization, and model evaluation. Multiple classification algorithms are benchmarked using cross-validation and performance analysis techniques to investigate their effectiveness across different text categories.

The work also explores transformer-based sentiment classification using BERT as a complementary approach.

